# round B77 (w236): the pool through 256 on two blocks of width 36 with 019's KL graph regularizer on the SECOND block at lambda 6.5e-4, ten times the 019 weight (6.5e-5, round 214 / w233, where the penalty is 0.76 of the data loss by epoch 40: the 025 sweep's lambda 1e-3 regime, the bottom of the range where a prior gained anything, the gain there starting at a ratio of 15). The new --graph-reg-lambda flag (2026-09-27). Paired against w232 and w233. Split into packs of THREE seeds (2026-09-27): the KL cell materializes the regularized block's attention, about 14.5 GB a seed on a 46 GB card, and six concurrent seeds ran out of memory (jobs 2900 and 2908 lost seeds 2703 to 2705). This pack carries seeds 2703 to 2705.
